    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.starter\n\n### Description\n\nWith certain colorschemes, EndOfBuffer may have a different background highlight compared to starter initial background, which disrupts overall visual consistency. \n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev+1102-geecddd241\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nWith lazy:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nreturn {\r\n  [[sainnhe/everforest]],\r\n  init = function()\r\n    vim.g.everforest_background = [[hard]]\r\n    vim.g.everforest_dim_inactive_windows = 1\r\n  end\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nPreserve current EndOfBuffer background highlight, overwrite it when displaying starter, and revert to its original state when exiting\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/b0bd5389-d5b1-44ef-b191-eef4f45ddbe7)\r\n",
